<launch>
  <!-- Tactile handover monitor: detects a human taking the held object.

         /auto_release_monitor/arm             handover/ArmMonitor  (side + session_token)
         /auto_release_monitor/disarm          std_srvs/Trigger
         /auto_release_monitor/<side>/arm      handover/ArmMonitor
         /auto_release_monitor/<side>/disarm   std_srvs/Trigger
         /auto_release_monitor/state           std_msgs/String (latched)
         /auto_release_monitor/ready           std_msgs/Bool   (latched)
         /auto_release_monitor/event           std_msgs/String  candidate/confirmed/fault

       One node per hand, like hand_control. DETECTION-ONLY BY DEFAULT: with
       release_integration:=false the node builds no release client at all, so
       it cannot open the hand and cannot ask the orchestrator to. Calibrate in
       this mode, then enable integration.

       It never opens the hand and never moves the arm in either mode. A
       verified pull becomes one request to /orchestrator/run_auto_release,
       which only validates and records the event for the task that owns the
       execution lock.

       OUT OF THE BOX THIS IS NOT_READY: the tactile schema is unconfirmed and
       the thresholds are uncalibrated. Arming is refused with the exact list.
       See handover/README.md.

       The orchestrator creates the session token and sends it with the arm
       request; this node echoes that same value in its release request and
       never generates one. Arming without a token is refused.

       roslaunch handover auto_release_monitor.launch side:=right
       rostopic echo -n1 /auto_release_monitor/ready
       rostopic echo /auto_release_monitor/event

       Running BOTH hands: the legacy unqualified service names would collide,
       so start the second node with advertise_legacy:=false once that argument
       is needed; today each node advertises both for backward compatibility.
  -->
  <arg name="side" default="right"/>
  <arg name="config" default="$(find handover)/config/auto_release.yaml"/>
  <arg name="release_integration" default="false"/>
  <arg name="rate" default="30.0"/>

  <node pkg="handover" type="auto_release_monitor.py" name="auto_release_monitor_$(arg side)"
        output="screen">
    <rosparam command="load" file="$(arg config)"/>
    <param name="side" value="$(arg side)"/>
    <param name="release_integration" type="bool" value="$(arg release_integration)"/>
    <param name="rate" value="$(arg rate)"/>
  </node>
</launch>
